On Wednesday, March 27, 2013 16:44:27 Nasya L'Bert wrote:
> coi ro do,  I have been wondering about the difference between using lo and
> ko and using cu.  For example, if I want to say "an American sells this
> tome" do the sentences "lo merko ku vecnu ti mi" and "lo merko cu vecnu ti
> mi" mean the same thing?

They mean the same, as does "lo merko ku cu vecnu ti mi". "lo merko cu ku 
vecnu ti mi" is ungrammatical, and "lo merko vecnu ti mi" is grammatical, but 
a sentence fragment.

Btw I thought you meant "lo merko cu vecnu lo vi paucku" when I had read just 
the English.

